{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that scvi-based RNA multiprofile models (~0.65 acc) substantially outperform singleprofile RNA models (~0.48-0.52 acc), but it is unclear whether the gain comes from multiprofile aggregation itself or from the scvi representation. config_002 tests pca_n2000 with multiprofile avgpool, directly comparing to config_001 while keeping the RNA encoder fixed. This isolates the effect of profile setting and aggregation, clarifies whether multiprofile helps even with a simpler encoder, and avoids adding image/fusion complexity before the RNA design space is better understood."
}

